---
import SiteFooter from '@/components/SiteFooter.astro'
import SiteHeader from '@/components/SiteHeader.astro'
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro'
import { PRICE, SITE } from '@/lib/site'

const updated = '3 August 2026'
---

<Base
  title={`Terms of sale: ${SITE.name}`}
  description="What a soquel licence grants, how the update window works, and how refunds are handled."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
    <SiteHeader />

    <main class="py-14 [&>h2]:mt-12 [&>h2]:font-mono [&>h2]:text-lg [&>h2]:font-medium [&>h2]:tracking-tight [&>p]:mt-4 [&>p]:leading-relaxed">
      <p class="label">Terms of sale</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-mono text-2xl leading-snug font-semibold tracking-tight">
        What you are buying, in plain terms.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-mute">
        These terms cover buying a soquel licence. They are deliberately short, and they say the
        same thing as the
        <a
          href="/pricing"
          data-umami-event="pricing-terms"
          class="text-ink underline underline-offset-4"
        >pricing page</a
        >: if the two ever disagree, this page is the one that binds.
      </p>
      <p class="text-mute">
        Using the application is governed separately by its source licence,
        <a
          href={SITE.licence}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="text-ink underline underline-offset-4"
        >FSL-1.1-MIT</a
        >, which applies whether you buy anything or not.
      </p>

      <h2>Who you are buying from</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        Soquel is made by {SITE.author}. Payment is handled by Polar as merchant of record: your
        payment, invoice and any applicable tax are between you and Polar, and your card details
        never reach us. The licence itself is granted by us, under these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>What a licence grants</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        A perpetual, non-exclusive right for one named person to use the official signed builds of
        soquel, on as many machines as that person works on, with no time limit and no requirement
        to stay connected or subscribed. A licence lifts the free tier's workspace tab limit; it
        does not unlock a separate edition, because there is only one.
      </p>
      <p class="text-mute">
        A licence is for one person. Two people working with soquel need two licences, whichever
        machines they use. Nothing in the software enforces that beyond the activation count, and we
        would rather say it plainly than pretend a technical measure decides it.
      </p>

      <h2>What it does not grant</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        Reselling, sublicensing or redistributing the signed builds, sharing your licence key or
        licence file outside the one person it was issued to, or removing the licence check from a
        build and distributing the result. The source licence covers what you may do with the code
        itself, including building it for your own use, which stays free.
      </p>

      <h2>The update window</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        A purchase includes {PRICE.months} months of updates, counted from the date of purchase.
        Every build released inside that window activates with your licence, whatever its version
        number, and keeps working indefinitely. When the window closes nothing is taken away: the
        last covered build stays fully licensed for as long as you care to run it.
      </p>
      <p class="text-mute">
        Installing a build released after your window is what the licence will not cover. The app
        says so and falls back to the free tier's limit, and going back to a covered build restores
        it. The comparison happens on your machine, against the date the build was made, with no
        network involved. A renewal at {PRICE.renewal} moves the window forward another {
          PRICE.months
        } months. Nothing renews automatically and we will never charge you without a new purchase.
      </p>
      <p class="text-mute">
        We do not commit to a release schedule, a number of releases, or any particular feature
        arriving inside your window. What we commit to is that anything we do release in it is
        yours.
      </p>

      <h2>Keys and activations</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        You receive a licence key on purchase. Activating it issues a signed licence file, up to {
          PRICE.activations
        } times per key; that file is what the application verifies, offline, from then on. You can
        release an activation from your Polar customer portal if you need another. Losing your key
        is recoverable, so ask rather than buying again.
      </p>
      <p class="text-mute">
        We may revoke a key in cases of fraud, chargeback or a shared key. Revoking prevents further
        activations; a licence file already issued keeps working, because a check that runs with the
        network unplugged cannot be withdrawn. That limit is documented in the file format published
        with the source, rather than left as a surprise.
      </p>

      <h2>Refunds</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        Within 14 days of purchase, for any reason, ask and you get your money back. No form and no
        justification needed. The application runs free with its tab limit, so you can judge it
        before paying, and a refund exists for when you did that and still got it wrong.
      </p>
      <p class="text-mute">
        Refunds are issued through Polar, who processed the payment. A refunded licence is revoked.
        If you are a consumer in the EU or UK, your statutory rights apply on top of this and
        nothing here reduces them.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        Soquel is provided as is, without warranty of any kind. It is a tool that connects to your
        databases and can change data when you tell it to; keep backups, and treat a destructive
        statement in soquel exactly as you would in a terminal. To the extent the law allows, our
        liability is limited to what you paid for your licence.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        These terms may change for future purchases. The terms in force on the day you bought are
        the ones that apply to your purchase, and the date below tells you which those were. Prices
        may change too, and a change never affects a licence already bought.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        Anything about a purchase, a refund or a lost key:
        <a
          href="mailto:hi@soquel.dev"
          data-umami-event="contact-terms"
          class="text-ink underline underline-offset-4"
        >hi@soquel.dev</a
        >. For how the application handles your data, see
        <a
          href="/privacy"
          data-umami-event="privacy-terms"
          class="text-ink underline underline-offset-4"
        >Privacy</a
        >.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-12 font-mono text-xs text-mute">Last updated {updated}.</p>
    </main>

    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</Base>
